Now I didn't beat the game, so I don't know for certain whether there's like a prescribed order of things, but like the way I was playing is because the game has like, sort of like each, each planet has some kind of mini puzzle in there.

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:44.440
Uh, you can just sort of go back and forth because you do have a device that if you go to the pause screen, you can just sort of teleport back to your ship and go somewhere else if you want.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:50.700
Um, you just sort of prod and poke and see like, oh, do I get this one yet?

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:56.360
Uh, because there are moments that I would just get stuck because I'm like, I am I soft locked?

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:58.080
Do I not have like a key item?

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:05.300
Uh, do I, do I not have a weapon that'll like, like for, for example, like break this like power barrier?

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:13.980
Um, and it turns out like, no, I just didn't do like, like a mini puzzle beforehand or like, oh, how do I get past this?

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:18.840
Uh, how do I get through this tunnel that is half the size of my sprite?

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:21.600
Right. And I just didn't know how to do that either.

00:14:22.360 --> 00:14:33.820
Um, so from what I could see, it's more so it's kind of, you can take it at whatever rhythm you want and, and it's just, you're going to get it or not get it.

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:44.640
And the whole changing of, uh, like which level you go to first, like maybe that's more so whichever one you feel like doing.

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:46.820
What were your thoughts on this?

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:59.940
Yeah. It's not Metroid like where, um, you unlock something and now, you know, you can go back and, and go to other planets and do things that you previously couldn't do or, um, or like sequence break.

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:04.360
Right. Like, oh, you know, if you, if you take it this order, you can skip this whole section entirely.

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:14.540
Like doesn't exist, but you don't have to follow a prescribed order other than, uh, starting on Siberia and Siberia.

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:19.200
Like not. Yeah. It's so close to the actual country, but it's cyber.

